<concept id="_Toc235706021" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Punctuation rules</title>
   <shortdesc>End every &lt;cmd&gt; with a period End every &lt;shortdesc&gt; with a period Use the Oxford</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Punctuation</keyword>
        <keyword>rules</keyword>
        <keyword>every</keyword>
        <keyword>period</keyword>
        <keyword>shortdesc</keyword>
        <keyword>Oxford</keyword>
        <indexterm>Punctuation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>rules</indexterm>
        <indexterm>every</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <conbody>
      <ul id="ul_11014337">
         <li>End every <codeph>&lt;cmd&gt;</codeph> with a period</li>
         <li>End every <codeph>&lt;shortdesc&gt;</codeph> with a period</li>
         <li>Use the Oxford comma: "concepts, tasks, and references"</li>
         <li>Do not use semicolons in procedure steps</li>
         <li>Use an em dash (—) for parenthetical clauses</li>
         <li>Do not use exclamation marks in technical documentation</li>
      </ul>
   </conbody>
</concept>
